      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "DeepStar Six (1989) emerged during the underwater sci-fi horror boom of the late 1980s, alongside <a href=\"/movie/2756\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"2756\">The Abyss</a> (1989) and <a href=\"/movie/14372\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"14372\">Leviathan</a> (1989). Director Sean S. Cunningham, famous for <a href=\"/movie/4488\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"4488\">Friday the 13th</a> (1980), transplanted slasher mechanics to the claustrophobic depths, following a deep-sea Navy installation team that awakens an ancient creature. The film channels Cold War submarine tensions like <a href=\"/movie/1669\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1669\">The Hunt for Red October</a> (1990) while incorporating creature features reminiscent of <a href=\"/movie/348\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"348\">Alien</a> (1979), particularly in its use of confined spaces and mounting paranoia."
      },
