      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "DeepStar Six's practical effects by Chris Walas (who worked on <a href=\"/movie/9426\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9426\">The Fly</a> (1986)) create genuine tension through minimal creature reveals - a technique that draws from <a href=\"/movie/578\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"578\">Jaws</a> (1975). The film's underwater base setting established a template followed by later subsea horror like <a href=\"/movie/443791\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"443791\">Underwater</a> (2020) and <a href=\"/movie/28450\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"28450\">The Rift</a> (1990), emphasizing isolation and technological failure as key sources of dread."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's military-industrial complex themes mirror contemporary fears about deep-sea exploitation, sharing DNA with eco-horror films like <a href=\"/movie/1255\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1255\">The Host</a> (2006). Its blend of monster movie tropes with hardware-heavy sci-fi anticipated later hybrid genres like <a href=\"/movie/8413\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"8413\">Event Horizon</a> (1997) and <a href=\"/movie/2787\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"2787\">Pitch Black</a> (2000). SUBHEAD: Legacy and Influence"
      },
      {
