      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "While not as technically accomplished as Cameron's <a href=\"/movie/2756\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"2756\">The Abyss</a> (1989), DeepStar Six helped establish underwater horror conventions that influenced films like <a href=\"/movie/12590\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"12590\">Below</a> (2002) and <a href=\"/movie/403119\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"403119\">47 Meters Down</a> (2017). Its emphasis on practical effects over CGI maintains its visceral impact, while its themes of deep-sea exploration dangers remain relevant in films like <a href=\"/movie/345940\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"345940\">The Meg</a> (2018)."
      }
